# Android — Compose standards

Complements `chinese-listener-architecture.mdc`, `chinese-listener-energy-efficiency.mdc`, and `docs/ANDROID_PRACTICES.md`.

## Build target

- **Platform:** Android only (single `:app` module unless user approves splits).
- **minSdk / targetSdk / compileSdk:** values in `app/build.gradle.kts` — do not change without approval.
- **UI:** **Jetpack Compose** + **Material 3**.

## Module

| Module | Responsibility |
|--------|----------------|
| `:app` | Activity, manifest, UI, presentation, domain, data, theme |

## Android window & OLED

- Manifest theme with **values** + **values-night** when applicable.
- `enableEdgeToEdge` with **opaque** status/navigation scrims aligned to light/dark when using edge-to-edge.
- Re-test on **physical device** when changing theme or edge-to-edge.

## Toolchain

- Kotlin / AGP / Compose: **only** versions declared in project Gradle files.
- JVM target: as set in `app/build.gradle.kts` — do not raise without approval.

## Compose checklist (every UI change)

- [ ] Wrapped in app theme composable
- [ ] Text uses explicit **onSurface** / **onPrimary** (or other `on*` matching background)
- [ ] State from presentation (`StateFlow` / ViewModel), not ad-hoc globals
- [ ] Events upward (UDF), no repository calls from composables
- [ ] `contentDescription` for meaningful images (null only for decorative)

## API level discipline

- No APIs above `minSdk` without guards or approved `minSdk` bump.
- Test permission/storage changes on a `minSdk` emulator or device.

## Verification

```bash
./gradlew :app:assembleDebug
./gradlew :app:testDebugUnitTest
```

Windows: `gradlew.bat`. Report unverified work honestly.
